  users.[33mmap[39m([33m([39mu) => ({ [36muserId[39m: u.id, [36mname[39m: u.name, [36memail[39m: u.email }))

  The consequence: renaming [38;5;153muserId[39m → [38;5;153muser_id[39m is a breaking change for every current [38;5;153mGET /users[39m consumer. [38;5;153mREADME.md[39m names
  three — the web app, the iOS app 3.2+, and the nightly partner export — and states that field names are part of the
  contract and that changes go through a versioned endpoint. The iOS and partner-export consumers in particular can't be
  redeployed in lockstep with the API. Nothing in this repo reads the field, so the repo won't tell you it broke; the
  clients will.

